{
  "id": "Compound::DB00331 - Gene::51079",
  "verbalization": "Metformin is implicated in the interaction with Ndufa13 through a shared pathway involving Nadh Dehydrogenase (ubiquinone) Activity. The evidence suggests that Metformin binds to Ndufa12 or Ndufv3, which in turn participate in the Nadh Dehydrogenase Activity. This activity is then participated by Ndufa13, establishing a potential functional link between Metformin and Ndufa13. The high scores from the three paths indicate a consistent and robust relationship, suggesting that Metformin may influence Ndufa13 through a mechanism involving the regulation of Nadh Dehydrogenase Activity. The overlapping pathways and the presence of multiple binding sites for Metformin support the idea that Ndufa13 is a downstream target in this metabolic interaction.",
